.TH OPTOLITHIUM 1 "October 2026" "Optolithium 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
optolithium \- optical lithography simulation and modeling software suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B optolithium
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-\-style\fR \fISTYLE\fR]
[\fB\-\-platform\fR \fIPLATFORM\fR]
[\fB\-\-maximized\fR|\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Optolithium
is an advanced optical lithography simulation and modeling suite for semiconductor microfabrication research and education.
It provides rigorous physical optical models including:
.IP \(bu 2
Source illumination modeling (coherent, annular, quadrupole, dipole, custom source shapes)
.IP \(bu 2
Pupil filtering and polarization effects
.IP \(bu 2
Partial coherent imaging and diffraction pattern calculation (Hopkins and Abbe formulations)
.IP \(bu 2
High\-NA vector imaging in thin and thick resist films
.IP \(bu 2
Photoactive compound (PAC) concentration latent image calculation (Dill ABC parameters)
.IP \(bu 2
Post\-exposure bake (PEB) thermal diffusion simulation
.IP \(bu 2
Resist development rate modeling (Mack, enhanced Mack, notch, and custom models) using fast marching eikonal solvers
.IP \(bu 2
Metrology analysis: critical dimension (CD), process window (Bossung curves, ED windows), exposure latitude, and depth of focus (DOF)
.PP
By default, running
.B optolithium
launches the graphical user interface. If an options file
(\fIFILE\fR)
is provided, it is loaded upon startup.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Path to an Optolithium simulation options file (\fI*.opl\fR) to load on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command\-line help summary and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display application version number and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
Set console logging verbosity level. Available levels:
\fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR, \fBCRITICAL\fR.
Default is \fBINFO\fR.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable verbose debug logging (equivalent to \fB\-\-log\-level DEBUG\fR).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational log messages, displaying only warnings and errors (equivalent to \fB\-\-log\-level WARNING\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR \fISTYLE\fR
Override Qt GUI application style (e.g., \fIFusion\fR, \fIWindows\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-platform\fR \fIPLATFORM\fR
Specify Qt GUI platform plugin (e.g., \fIxcb\fR, \fIwayland\fR, \fIoffscreen\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-maximized\fR
Start the main application window maximized.
.TP
\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
Start the main application window in full screen mode.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBOPTOLITHIUM_HOME\fR
Directory where Optolithium stores user configuration, material databases, and cache. Defaults to \fI~/.Optolithium\fR.
.TP
\fBOPTOLITHIUM_VENV\fR
Path to an external Python virtual environment to use instead of the bundled runtime.
.TP
\fBQT_QPA_PLATFORM\fR
Overrides the default Qt platform abstraction plugin (e.g., set to \fIoffscreen\fR for headless test runs).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.Optolithium/config.json\fR
User preferences and application configuration file.
.TP
\fI~/.Optolithium/OptolithiumDatabase.db\fR
SQLite database containing material refractive indices, resist formulations, and simulation presets.
.TP
\fI~/.Optolithium/map.json\fR
GDSII layer transmittance and phase mapping configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start Optolithium GUI:
.B optolithium
.TP
Open an existing simulation project:
.B optolithium my_simulation.opl
.TP
Print version:
.B optolithium \-\-version
.TP
Run with debug logging:
.B optolithium \-\-debug
